From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bluetoothapis, winebth.sys: remote devices, services, rename, remove, discoverable (3567)

bluetoothapis, winebth.sys: remote devices, installed services, service state, rename, remove, discoverable

winebth.sys gets two control codes on a radio's device (include/wine/winebth.h): the devices BlueZ knows of
for the adapter (a fresh private D-Bus connection per request: GetManagedObjects, the Device1 objects of the
adapter with address, alias, class, paired/connected/trusted, RSSI and service UUIDs), and changes (Adapter1
RemoveDevice, Device1 Alias, ConnectProfile/DisconnectProfile, Adapter1 Discoverable).
bluetoothapis uses them: BluetoothFindFirstDevice/NextDevice/DeviceClose with the search flags (authenticated =
paired, remembered = paired or trusted, unknown = not remembered, connected; an inquiry is not started),
BluetoothGetDeviceInfo, BluetoothEnumerateInstalledServices (the device's service UUIDs),
BluetoothSetServiceState (connect or disconnect the profile), BluetoothUpdateDeviceRecord (the name),
BluetoothRemoveDevice, BluetoothEnableDiscovery and BluetoothIsVersionAvailable (the first radio's LMP version).
Addresses are BLUETOOTH_ADDRESS as on Windows (the least significant byte first).
---
